{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"I found the problem, fixed it and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned a 200 response.\n\nThe `orders-validator` consumer had stopped at offset 20 of the `orders-fulfillment` topic. That record wasn't valid JSON, and the consumer paused on it indefinitely, so the backlog of orders grew while `order-stream` kept producing.\n\nI edited `consumer.py` in the `orders-pipeline-scripts` ConfigMap so a bad record is logged, copied to a new `orders-processed-dlq` topic, and skipped. Then I restarted `orders-validator`. It is processing orders again; the last log line showed offset 68.\n\nI didn't confirm that end-user request success and latency are back to normal. The one observable symptom I found was the stalled consumer, and I haven't checked whether that is what end users were hitting."}}
